  "course_description": "Focus on selected topics in East Asian studies.",
  "course_notes": "(Freshmen Seminar - Limited to First Year Students Only) (Human beings are collections of stories. They accumulate stories over a lifetime, and when they are given the opportunity, they select an appropriate story and tell it. Human memory is story-based; and as such, we know what we tell, and we tell what we know. In this course, we will explore how our attachment to stories shapes the ways we utilize our memories and produce history as both individuals and members of various communities. By experimenting on their own life stories, students will identify and better understand how their self-identities operate as storytelling practices.)",
